Subject: The dead-end abort may fire only when the baseline tier fails

What this does
  The dead-end abort may fire only when the baseline tier fails.

Why we need it
  `REGVM_VERIFY_DEAD_END` aborted in `js_regvm_encode` when the optimising pass refused a shape a second time -- before the baseline tier ran. That refusal now *selects* the baseline, so a non-`NDEBUG` build aborted on any large call site, wide `switch`, 5,000-parameter function or 70,000-property literal: 21 of the 189 generated programs killed the host.

What it adds
  The abort is removed from the optimising refusal (it reports and defers) and moved to the baseline tier's own refusal path, which is the only remaining place the invariant can fire. A release build is unchanged (`REGVM_VERIFY_DEAD_END` is a no-op there).

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index e8bd27a..798f1f7 100644
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -58282,7 +58282,6 @@ static int regvm_ctl_bound(JSContext *ctx, const JSRegIR *ir, const uint8_t *bc,
     return rc;
 }
 
-
 /* Move origins that are not a stack-VM opcode. */
 #define REGVM_ORIG_LOWER 0xFE   /* lowering, opcode not recorded */
 #define REGVM_ORIG_PHI   0xFD   /* an edge's parallel copy */
@@ -69250,7 +69249,8 @@ static __exception int js_regvm_build_cfg(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionDef *fd,
                 rc = 0;
                 goto done;
             }
-            REGVM_VERIFY_DEAD_END(enc_why ? enc_why : "the encoder refused");
+            /* Refused twice: `*pdeferred = 1` hands the function to the
+               baseline tier. The dead-end check belongs to the baseline. */
             regvm_report_refusal(ctx, fd, enc_why ? enc_why : "?");
             *pdeferred = 1;
             deferred = 1;
@@ -70337,10 +70337,10 @@ static __exception int js_regvm_build_baseline(JSContext *ctx, JSFunctionDef *fd
         if (rc)
             goto done;
         if (refused) {
-            /*
-             * The baseline is the last tier; a refusal here is a modelling gap
-             * the caller must surface, not a shape to hand on.
-             */
+            /* The baseline is the last tier: a refusal here is a modelling gap
+               the caller must surface, and the only point where the dead-end
+               check may fire under QJS_REGVM_VERIFY. */
+            REGVM_VERIFY_DEAD_END(why ? why : "the baseline refused");
             if (regvm_report_deferred_on())
                 fprintf(stderr, "regvm: BASELINE refused: %s\n",
                         why ? why : "?");
